course: dictionary
lesson: 8385
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rubbish is a good example. «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» Bins hold things we throw away, so here rubbish means things we no longer want. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Things to throw away is the best fit.
explain: Now read this: «I'm rubbish at drawing.» You cannot put a bin into this sentence, so the meaning must be different. Rubbish here means very bad. Test it by swapping in your meaning: «I'm very bad at drawing» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Rubbish can also mean nonsense. «Stop talking rubbish» means stop saying silly or untrue things. The same word can even do a different job: to rubbish an idea means to say the idea is worthless. Read the words around the word, and they will tell you which meaning to choose.
fact: Rubbish means things you throw away because they are no longer wanted or useful.
fact: «Rubbish» can also mean nonsense, something silly or untrue.
fact: «Rubbish» (informal, British) means very bad, as in «I'm rubbish at drawing».
fact: To rubbish an idea is to say it is worthless.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, rubbish is the usual word; in the USA people say «trash» or «garbage».
exercise: «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» What does rubbish mean here? | *Things we throw away | Nonsense, silly or untrue | To say an idea is worthless | Very bad
exercise: «I'm rubbish at drawing.» What does rubbish mean here? | Clean and tidy | Things we throw away | *Very bad | Silly and untrue
exercise: Ella says, «Stop talking rubbish!» What does rubbish mean? | *Nonsense, silly or untrue things | A rubbish tip | Things we throw away | Very bad at talking
test: Sam says, «Let's take the rubbish out.» What does rubbish mean? | Silly, untrue things | To say an idea is worthless | *Things we throw away | Very bad at jobs
test: Priya says, «Your plan is rubbish, it will never work.» Which meaning fits? | *Silly and not worth anything | Things we throw away | Able to be recycled | Very good and clever
exam: In «Smoke from vehicles, factories and burning rubbish pollutes the air», what does rubbish mean? | To say an idea is worthless | *Things we throw away | Very bad | Nonsense, silly or untrue things
